Rasool Allah ﷺ tells us in a long Hadith(حديث) about the story of the soul, where it leaves the body; the chip that the soul takes. He says; When the believer is dying; the angels come down with a coffin from Jannah(جنة), and some scent from Jannah(جنة), and they descend, and they sit in front of that person, and then the Angel of Death descends and tells the believer; be happy and pleased with the Promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for you. And then he calls the soul to come out. He says;

Oh, you soul in the state of tranquility! Come out to the pleasure that will be provided to you by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. So Rasool Allah ﷺ says; that soul would come out so easily. It is like a drop of water that is flowing down from a Jerk(جرك); like pouring a drop of water. It slides so easily out of the body. And as soon as the angel of death takes that soul; all of the angels would jump. Every one of them wants to take the honour of holding that soul and wrapping it in the coffin. And then they would carry it up in the heavens. And Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Whenever they would carry it next to a group of angels; they would smell this beautiful scent and they would say; Whose soul is this? And the angels will tell them; This is the soul of so and so. They would call him with his best names. Until, they reach to the gates of the lowest heaven. And then they would seek permission, so the gates of that heaven will open up. And whenever this soul is being carried through a heaven; the angels of that heaven will accompany it until the next heaven. And angels are surrounding this soul all the way up, until it reaches to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will deliver the Promise of Jannah(جنة) to that soul. And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will say; Take that soul back to Earth; because that is where I've created them from, and that is where they would return, and that is where they would be resurrected from. So the soul would then descend down with honour of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. And then Rasool Allah ﷺ tells us, what happens to the soul of the non-believer or the evil doer. Rasool Allah ﷺ says; The angels come down with a coffin from hellfire, and they come next to him, and the angel of death would stand next to him and say;

Oh, you evil soul! Come out to the punishment of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and his anger. So that soul would disperse around the body, and try to cling to every nerve and muscle. It doesn't want to leave. So the Angel of Death is pulling that soul out. Rasool Allah ﷺ says; The pain of that soul; is like a branch filled with thorns being pulled out of a wet ball of wool. Imagine! Pulling out a branch filled with thorns out of a wet ball of wool. It is tearing apart the nerves and the muscles of that person; pain and agony of death. And as soon as that soul comes out; all of the angels would jump and would wrap it up in a coffin from hellfire, and then they would carry it out. Rasool Allah ﷺ says; It has a stinking rotten smell. And whenever this soul passes next to angels, they would start cursing it, and they would say; Whose soul is this? So the angels would call him with his worst name. And then, the angels would carry it up to the first heaven; As-Sama'ad-Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); the lowest heaven; and they would seek permission, but the door of that Heaven will not open.

The doors of the heavens will not be open for them. And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Throw that soul to the lowest Earth! Throw that soul down to the lowest Earth! So that soul will be thrown down with the disgrace by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. Now the soul is in the grave. So we start with the next section in Al-Akhirah(الآخرة), and that is; Al-Qabr(القبر); The Grave. Uthman Ibn Affan رضى الله عنه; whenever he would see a grave; he would cry. So they ask him; How come when you remember Jannah(جنة); Nar(نار), that wouldn't affect you like when you remember the grave; Al-Qabr(القبر)? Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said;

Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said; I heard, Rasool Allah ﷺ say; that the grave is the first step towards Akhirah(آخرة). It's the first step of Akhirah(آخرة). If you make it through it; then whatever comes after it will be easier. And if you cannot make it through the grave; then whatever will happen after; it is worse. And that is why, I cry, whenever I remember the grave. And then he said that Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Everything horrific that I have seen; the grave is more horrific. Everything that I've seen in my life; nothing is as worse as what I have seen in the grave. And soon, we're going to be there. Every one of us; we're going to leave the comfort of this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). We're going to leave it behind. We're going to leave it behind, and we're going to be there. Every single one of us; one day, will be carried and will be put in that hole in the earth. The grave is dark. There was a woman who used to clean the Masjid(مسجد). In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ; an old woman; she would come and clean the Masjid(مسجد). She was ill, and then she died late at night. So the Sahabahرضى الله عنهم; they buried her. And they did not wake up Rasool Allah ﷺ, because it was late at night. And then later Rasool Allah ﷺ asked; Where is that old women? They said; She became ill and we buried her. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Why didn't you call me? Rasool Allah ﷺ was the Father for this ummah(امة). He cared about every single one of them. The weak and the strong; the man and the woman; the old and the young. He said; Why don't you wake me up? And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Show me her grave. So he went and visited her grave, and then he said;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; these graves are dark, but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is going to give them light because of my Salah(صلوة) on them; narrated by Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ). Graves are dark, but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is going to give them light because of my Salah(صلوة) on them. And the grave as soon as it needs you; because you belong there. You're from the earth. So as soon as you're put in the grave; the grave will squeeze you and hug you. It seems like a hug but it's a painful squeeze. because you're part of the earth. That's where you created from. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; The grave squeezes; if anyone would have been saved from this squeeze; it would have been Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ). Even Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ); the Wali(ولي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the grave squeezed him. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ); this is the man, whom the Arsh(عرش) of Allah; the Throne of Allah shake for his death. This is the man, whom the doors of heavens open up for, and this is the man who of 70,000 angels accompanied in his Janazah(جنازه); but the grave squeezed him, but then it released him. Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ); the Arsh(عرش) of Allah; the Throne of Allah shaked for the death of Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), and the doors of heaven were opening to welcome the soul of Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), and 70,000 angels came down, specially to accompany the Janazah(جنازه) of Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), because Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) is the leader of Al Ansaar(ألأنْصَار); one of their leaders who opened up Madinah(مَدِينَه) for Rasool Allah ﷺ, and he is one of the ones who hosted Rasool Allah ﷺ, and was the best host. And he is one of the people who defended Rasool Allah ﷺ until he died. And that is the honour that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave him. Nevertheless, he was still squeezed in the grave. Rasool Allah ﷺ once said; If anybody is going to be saved from the squeezing of the grave; it would be this young child. There was a child who was buried; even that child was squeezed by the grave. So we start talking now about Fitnat-ul-Qabr(فِتْنَةُالْقَبر); the trials and the tribulations of the grave. Trials and the tribulations of the grave, it's called Fitnat-ul-Qabr(فِتْنَةُالْقَبر). And Rasool Allah ﷺ mentions in a Hadith(حديث) about the questioning of the person in the grave. As soon as a person gets into the grave; two angels; Munkar-an-Nakeer(مُنْكَرَالنَّكِير) would descend on that person. Fayantahirani(فينتهران). And they would scream at him, and they would shock that person and surprise him; meaning that the way of conversation with these two angels is not very sort of say; polite. They're very tough, strong, and they expect from you a straight answer immediately. Whether you are a believer or not; they're going to come in that fashion. …. is when they come, and scream at a person, and speak to him loudly, and straightforwardly. So these two angels will come down; Munkar-an-Nakeer(مُنْكَرَالنَّكِير); and they would ask three questions.

Who is your Lord? What is your religion? And who's your prophet? Only three questions. This is the examination. This is the test. This is the test we should prepare for. And this test has only three questions in it. We study years, for tests. How much time are we given for this most important test that we're going to face in our life? We know the questions, and we know the answers. Who is your Lord? What is your religion? And who's your prophet? Three questions! And they expect from you, straightforward, immediate answer. The believer would say;

My Lord Is Allah, and my religion is Islam, and my prophet is Muhammadﷺ. They would hear a sound coming from above; saying, My servant is telling the truth. So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is verifying the answers. The angels are asking the questions, and then Allah is verifying; if the answers you're saying are the truth or not. And that is where Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Qur'an;

Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sets firm the believers on the firm statement in this world. And what is the firm statement?

That is the firm, and established statement. That is the truth, that is the reality. So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will set the believer firm on; With the non-believer or the Munafiq(منافق); the angels would come down, and they would say; Who's your Lord? What's your religion? And who's your prophet? When they would ask him about the Prophet, they would say; What? I don't know? I heard the people say this, and I said it. They would smash him with a hammer that will turn him into dust. That person is saying, what he heard. I don't know! But I heard people say this about Muhammadﷺ. I heard Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) say this about him. I heard Abu Lahab(ابو لهب). I heard ABC News. I heard CNN. I read in the newspaper. I was listening to the stereotypes about Muhammadﷺ; this is what I heard. That's not the answer; the angels want to hear from you. They want to hear from you; Muhammadﷺ is my Nabi(نَبِي). So it needs to be clear that the Eeman(ايمان) and Muhammadﷺ is one of the pillars, that you will be asked about in your grave. So it's not sufficient to believe in one God; you must believe in the representatives of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and those are the messengers of Allah. Muhammadﷺ, Eesa(عيسى), Musa(موسى), Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم); we have to believe in the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; because they are the ones, who are conveying the message of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to the people in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). So we have to have Eeman(ايمان). Here you say, stereotyping that the people here about Muhammadﷺ, they will mention it in the grave, but will not be a valid answer. And this is the test in the grave. And Rasool Allah ﷺ says; This is the last test the believer will go through; the last …. This is the final one. After that test, it's over with. There's no more tests. Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ) narrates that; Asmaa' binte Abi Bakr(اسماء بنت ابى بكر) says; Rasool Allah ﷺ stood in the Masjid(مسجد) and delivered a speech, and he started talking about the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the grave;

Until there was an uproar in the Masjid(مسجد). Rasool Allah ﷺ was speaking about the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the grave. Asmaa'(اسماء) says; there was an uproar in the Masjid(مسجد); loud noises. What was that noise? The Sahabahرضى الله عنهم were crying. Asmaa'(اسماء) said; I couldn't hear the Khutbah(خطبه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ. And I waited until the noise calmed down. And then I asked a man, next to me;

May Allah bless you! What is the last thing Rasool Allah ﷺ said? Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Rasool Allah ﷺ said; It has been revealed to me, that you will go through Fitnah(فِتْنَه); trials in your graves, similar to the fitna of Ad-Dajjal(الدّجال). The extreme situation and danger of the trials and tribulations of the grave, are similar to the trials and the tribulations of Ad-Dajjal(الدّجال). And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

There is no Fitnah(فِتْنَه); there is no trial; since Adam(آدَم) was created until the day of judgment; more severe than the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) Ad-Dajjal(الدّجال). And every one of us will go through something similar to that in our graves. Me and you; this is what it's talking about. It's not talking about someone else. Me and you; pretty soon are going to go through that Fitnah(فِتْنَه). And we will be questioned, and we will go through that test and trial and tribulation. When the Sahabahرضى الله عنهم heard this; there was an uproar in the Masjid(مسجد), because of their crying and weeping. Because their hearts were soft. For us; we are not affected. And if we are affected; it's a very, very temporary effect. Very soon it will be eliminated. One of us could witness a Janazah(جنازه); and I've seen this; we could go to a Janazah(جنازه), and we can see the grave with our eyes, and see the end of the human being, when he is dumped in a hole; we could see that with our own eyes. And then, in the cemetery; we could be joking and laughing together. I've seen that. We are facing death; seeing the end of the human life; and we could be telling jokes and laughing; this is, Qaswat-ul Qalb(قسوةالقلب); this is a heart similar to rock. It's just like a solid rock; it's not soft. The Sahabahرضى الله عنهم; they just heard Rasool Allah ﷺ speaking about the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the grave, Asmaa'(اسماء) said; I couldn't hear anything,

There was an uproar of loud voices in the Masjid(مسجد). I had to wait, until it calmed down for me to know what Rasool Allah ﷺ said. We're suffering from a disease. That is a disease and illness, that we need to cure. This disease is worse than a medical heart problem. It's worse. And if we are suffering from a medical heart problem; we would spend our life; and we would spend our time; and our effort to cure it. But if we're suffering from diseases like this; we let them go; we let them in our hearts; we don't even worry about it. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ said; This ummah(امة) will go through tests in the grave. And if it wasn't for the fact that you would not bury your dead; I would have asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to allow you to hear; what's happening underground. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I can hear; I can hear what's happening underground, and I would ask Allah to allow you to hear it. But I'm afraid, if I do so; you would not dare to bury your dead. If you're able to hear what's happening under the surface; you would not bury any dead person. You would keep them on the surface of the earth; you're not going to put them there. Because of the horror of what's happening underground. Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says that, not only Rasool Allah ﷺ heard this, but he said; we know of some people who also hear this. He said; we have heard accounts of people hearing the punishment in the grave. And if we have heard accounts of people, seeing dead bodies coming out from the grave being punished, and they're screaming, and the scars are on their body. Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says; when you're asleep; your soul is separate from the body. Nevertheless, sometimes in a dream; the dream could be so intense that your body could start moving and acting upon that dream, and it could start walking in that dream, acting and moving and running, even though your eyes are closed. Even though the soul is separate from the body when you're asleep. Because, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

Allah is the One who takes away your souls when you are sleeping. So the soul is taken out of the body in the state of sleep. Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says the same thing. Sometimes the punishment could be so intense and severe, that the body starts acting upon that punishment. And you could see dead people coming out from the graves; running and the angels are following them and torturing them. The description of the punishment of the grave, and the reward of the grave; after the questioning of the believer; when the believer is given the right answers; a voice calls from the heaven;

My servant is telling the truth.

So furnish his grave from Paradise, and provide him with clothes from Paradise, and open for him a gate to Paradise. This grave on Earth, is hooked up to Jannah(جنة); is directly connected to paradise. This grave in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) of the believer; it has a direct connection to Jannah(جنة); there's a gate. And this person in the grave, is able to see his place in Jannah(جنة). He's not able to go there, but he can see it. And then, a very handsome person would walk in the grave; very pleasant face. So the dead person would say; who are you? That person would say; I am your good deeds, and I came to spend time with you, and be with you until the day of judgment. I will be with you; you're not going to be alone. And that's why, one of a At-Taba'een(ألتابعين); he had a student. He told his student; you have studied under me for 30 years. Tell me what have you learned? 30 years you studying under me. Tell me, what have you learned throughout this period? That man said; I learned eight things. One of these things, he said; I learned, that every one of us has some loved ones, and we have some love things, some of these love things we're going to leave, when we're still in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). And some of these love things we're going to leave at home. And some of these loved ones or things are going to come with us to our graves. But then when we go to the grave, no one will be with us. No loved one or loved thing will be with us in our graves; except for our good deeds, that's why I have taken my good deeds to be the most beloved thing to me. I'm going to leave my family; I'm going to leave wealth; I'm going to leave my car; I'm going to leave my home behind; I'm going to leave everything. The only thing that I can take with me in my grave is my good deeds. Therefore, let me have a lot of them. And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; he will have a window showing paradise, and a window showing hellfire. And he will be told; this is where you could have been, if you were not a believer; in hellfire. And this is what you've got, because of your Eeman(ايمان). When he sees that, he will say;

Oh Allah! Start the day of judgment. When he sees what's waiting for him in Jannah(جنة), he says; Oh Allah! Bring the Day of Judgment, So that I can go to my family and to my wealth. Where is his family and wealth? Is it in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)? His family and wealth now is in Akhirah(آخرة). He is not caring now about what he has left behind in this world. He doesn't want to go back to this world. He will not regret it. Now he's in a hurry. He wants to go to what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has reserved for him in Jannah(جنة).

Oh Allah! Let the day of judgment start; as soon as possible, so that I can go and be with my family and my wealth. Al-Kafir(كافر), Wa-al-Fajir(الفاجر); The corrupt person, the evil person, or the non believer; Rasool Allah ﷺ says; After the questioning,

An announcement will be made from the heavens, that he is a liar.

Furnish his grave from hellfire, and give him close from hellfire, and open him a gate to hellfire. This grave that you see in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is directly connected to Hell fire. So we have graves under the surface of the Earth. We think are part of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); we don't know that they are connected to Al-Akhirah(الآخرة). We don't know that the people of Jannah(جنة) are seeing Jannah(جنة) from their graves, and the people of hellfire are seeing hellfire from their graves. And then an evil, ugly looking person would come in the grave. So the man would say; who are you? What an evil person you are? He would say; I am your evil deeds, and I will be with you until the day of judgment. And he has a stinking, rotten smell that will be with him until the day of judgment. And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Two windows will be open; the window to Jannah(جنة) and a window in hellfire. He would be told; this is where you could have been, if you were a believer, that's the regret. So he's not always suffering physically, but he's suffering psychologically because of regret. And this is, where you will be in hellfire. He would say;

Oh Allah! Do not let the day of judgment start. Can the Muslim be punished in his grave? Yes. Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says; Al- Imam Al-Qurtubi(الاِمَام ألقرطبي) says; Realize, that the punishment of the grave is not solely for the non believers, and is not only for the hypocrites, but also it could happen to some of the believers, because of their shortcomings in their deeds. So it can happen to a believer, due to shortcomings in their actions. So what are some of the reasons, that could cause the punishment of the grave? There is general reason, and that is shortcomings in general. That's a general reason. But then, there are a few specific reasons. Number one; theft; stealing; taking something that doesn't belong to you and cheating. There was a servant with Rasool Allah ﷺ, and they were out in Jihad(جهاد), and this servant was preparing the saddle for Rasool Allah ﷺ when a stray arrow killed him. So the Muslims started saying;

Congratulations for him! He is got Jannah(جنة). Because he died in the battle field; Shaheed(شَهِيد). Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Rasool Allah ﷺ said; No! In the Name of Allah; the cloak which he stole in the day of Khaybar(خَيْبَر) is wrapped around him and is burning him in his grave. This man is out in Jihad(جهاد). He is fighting the sake of Allah; and he died in that battle. And the Muslim said, he is a Shaheed(شَهِيد). Rasool Allah ﷺ said; No! the cloak which he stole on the day of Khaybar(خَيْبَر); just a cloak; a cloth; piece of cloth; he took it without taking permission. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; that cloth is wrapped around him and is burning him in his grave. Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! For a cloak. What about the ones who are raking 1000s and 1000s or millions of dollars? This is a piece of cloth. And that person is being punished in his grave because of piece of cloth. What about the ones who cheat millions of dollars, and steal millions of dollars and take and abuse the rights of the Muslims and steal their money by cheating? What will happen to them in their graves, for a miser return? What is it for? For a temporary enjoyment in this life. Any money that is taken unlawfully; there is no Barakah(بركة) in it. And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى would inflict you with diseases and with disasters, which will eventually cause you to spend all of your money on, because that money doesn't have Barakah(بركة). Monetary Transactions; is something that could cause you great rewards or great punishment. It all depends on the way you use it. It's a test from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to test you; are you going to be grateful or ungrateful.

Number two and three; Rasool Allah ﷺ in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Bukhari(بخاريْ); Passed by two graves. And Rasool Allah ﷺ said; The two men in his graves are being punished. They're suffering now. But Rasool Allah ﷺ said; They are not suffering because of something major. One of them used to slander; Annamimah(النّميمه), and the other one would not purify himself and clean himself from urine. and they were being punished in their graves because of that. one of them would slander; Annamimah(النّميمه). He would go and take cause disunity among the people, and slander his brothers or sisters. And the other one would not make Taharah(طهارة); would not cleanse himself, because we know that cleanliness is part of Eeman(ايمان). Number four, five, six, and seven are mentioned in one Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ). Rasool Allah ﷺ sometimes after Fajr(فجر), when he would finish  the Salah(صلوة); he would turn around and ask the Sahabah(صحابه); Did any of you see a dream? If they saw any dreams; he would interpret it for them. One day, he asked them; Did you see any dreams? They said; No. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; But I, when I was asleep. Two men came down, and they grabbed me by my hand. And we know that the dreams of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are, Wahi(وحى); revelation; they're true. So Rasool Allah ﷺ says; When I was asleep; two men came down, and they grabbed my hand, and they took me with them. So he passed by a man sitting down, and someone is throwing iron hooks in his mouth, and they're tearing up his mouth, and they're coming out from the end from his neck. Two large hooks; they're going in his mouth, and they're coming out from the other side. I said; Who is this? They didn't answer. They took me with them to another place. So I saw someone. So they carried me with them. And there was someone laying on his back, and someone standing over him with a rock; big rock in his hands, and he would throw it on the man lying down and crushed his head, and then the rock; the stone, would roll. So by the time he goes and picks up the rock; the head would grow up again, and then he would smash it again. And he would keep on doing that consistently. I told them; what is this? They didn't answer. And then we passed next to an oven, that looked like a cone. So it was narrow from the top, and wide from the bottom; a cone; which was an oven. And there were some men and women inside. And those men and women, fire would erupt from beneath them, and it would burn them, so they would scream and try to climb out of the oven, but because it's like cone; they keep on sliding down into the fire. I said; What is this? They didn't answer. And then we went and saw a river of blood. And there's someone swimming in that river. And whenever he wants to get out of the river of blood; there's someone standing on the shore, and would throw a big rock in his mouth that would push him back in the river. And he would try to come out again, and then he would throw another rock in his mouth, and it would push him back to the river of blood. I said; What is this? And then they took me with them to a green, beautiful garden. In the middle of the garden; there was a huge tree. Next to the tree, there was an old man surrounded with many children. And then there was another man on the side. He had fire between his hands, and he was igniting the fire and making it burn even more. And then they took me up the tree. And we went on that tree into a room. I have never seen a room more beautiful than that room. And in that room; there were old men and young men, old women and young women and children. And then they took me out of that room, and they carried me up to a room that is even more beautiful. And I went in there, and I saw some young men and old men. I told them; What is this? So they told me; The man that had hooks in his mouth that would tear it up to his neck; is the man who tells a lie, and that lie will be carried all around the world. So this is his punishment until the day of judgment. We think about how a lie can reach the whole world. Now, with media and mass media; you could lie, and that lie could be carried all over the world. And when a lie comes out the mouth; it cannot be taken back. It's like trying to put the camel through a needle eye. If it comes out of the mouth; it's done. So that person would say; tell a lie. He cannot control it, and goes all around the world. So this is his punishment until the day of judgment. That's the punishment of Kadhib(كَذِبْ); lying.

Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) says that, Rasool Allah ﷺ said that; Lying leads to corruption; and corruption leads to hellfire; and a man would keep on lying until Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Would write him down as a liar. And then they said; the man that was lying down, and his head was being crushed with a big stone; that is the person who learned Qur'an, but then, would not follow it during the daytime, and would not recite it in the nighttime. So this is a person who learned Qur'an; studied Qur'an; or memorized Qur'an, but he would not pray and recite Qur'an at night, and he would not follow up on the commandments of Qur'an in the daytime. So Qur'an is just as they say now; Barakah(بركة). It has no use. It's in the heart, but there is no action based on Qur'an. We know Qur'an, and we don't follow it. And that is the punishment for it. Qur'an is a blessed book. There is Barakah(بركة) in Qur'an. But the Barakah(بركة) comes by following the commandments of Qur'an. It does not come by wrapping Qur'an in digital cloths, and putting it on the rack until dust builds on it. Qur'an is in the heart. And those men and women, who were in the oven; those are Az-Zuna(الزنا); the ones who used to commit Zina(زنا); adultery and fornication. And that's their punishment until the day of judgment. And the one who was swimming in the river of blood, and then would be pushed in it with a rock; that's the one who used to deal with interest. And that is his punishment until the Day of Judgment. It is punishment in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). It's punishment in the grave. It's punishment on youm-al-Qayamah(يوم القيامة). And it's punishment in hell fire. And there is no pleasure in it in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). And there is no use in it in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

The eventual ending of Riba'(رباء) is decrease. And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will destroy Riba'(رباء). That's in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Akhirah(آخرة). And then, this is the punishment of the person, who deals with interest, in the grave; swimming in a river of flood. And then, on the day of judgment; Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says; The one who used to deal with Riba'(رباء), when he comes out of his grave; the angels will give him weapons, and they will tell him; Go and fight with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Qur'an;

If you deal with interest; then there is an announced and waged war against you by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will wage this war on you on the Day of Judgment, and to be fair with you; He Will give you weapons to fight with him with. That is the result of Riba'(رباء). And then, in Akhirah(آخرة); eventually it is Hellfire;

That is the result of dealing with Riba'(رباء); interest. We try to look for ways around it. We go shopping for Fatwa(فتوى), to get around the Riba'(رباء). This is the Hukum(حكم) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has not waged war except on two people; the one who fights the Awliya(اولياء) of Allah.

The one who fights my Awliya(اولياء); then I would wage war against them. And the second person is the one, who deals with interest.

These are the only two people, whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has announced war against. And then the old man sitting next to the tree; is Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), and the children surrounding him; are the children who died in young age. And the man who was burning the fire; is the guardian of hellfire; Maalik(مالك). And the room that you saw on the tree; is the room reserved for the believers; the men and women. And then the room that was above it; is the room of  Ash-Shuhadaa(اَشُّهَدآء). And I am Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), and this is Michael(ميكائيل). Now look up, so Rasool Allah ﷺ looked up at the sky, and Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I saw way up in the sky, what appeared to be like clouds. They told me; that is your home. I told them; Let me visit my home. They said; No, you still have some life to spend on Earth; when it's over; then you can visit your home. That house, on the tree, is for the believers, who die in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا). But the house above it; the room above it; is for Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء). The honour that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given to the Shaheed(شَهِيد). And then way up; it cannot even be seen by the eyes, is a place Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has reserved for the leader of mankind; Muhammadﷺ. There are few other things that could cause punishment in the grave like, being in debt. You owe someone money. And there's a Hadith(حديث) where, one of the Sahabah(صحابه) passed away, so Rasool Allah ﷺ told his brother; Go and pay the debt of your brother, because your brother is being held from Jannah(جنة) with his debt. You cannot go to Jannah(جنة), until his debt releases him. So the debt is surrounding that Sahabi(صحابي), and he cannot go to Jannah(جنة) until, it's paid off. So Rasool Allah ﷺ told his brother; Paid off; paid off your brother's debt. There's also something that could cause harm to the dead. And that is the, excessive weeping of his or her family. If you pass away and your family weep on you excessively, that could cause some pain. Because, when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was injured and he was passing away; Sohaib(صهيب); companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ was Sahabi(صحابي) Sohaib(صهيب), Ar-Rumi(الرّومى); he came and he saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),  and he started to cry. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

The dead person would suffer, because of the crying and weeping of his family. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want anybody to weep on him. Tears falling down and crying is okay; that's natural. We would feel sorrow and sadness, when a loved one passes away. But it should not be excessive, and lose patience. No! Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to see us patient. The tears would drop from guys of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when a loved one passed away. But Rasool Allah ﷺ would never allow himself or any of the Sahabah(صحابه), to excessively weep on anyone. What saves from the punishment of the grave? Number one; the good deeds. Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث); When the dead person is buried; he's able to hear the footsteps of the people, when they're leaving his cemetery. And then, his good deeds would surround him. So Salah(صلوة) would come next to his head, fasting would come on his right side, and Zaka'ah(زكوة) would come on the left side, and then the other good deeds would come next to his feet. So whenever this person would be attacked from the head; the Salah(صلوة) would say; No, you cannot come from this side. And whenever the attack is from the right side; the Siyam(صيام) would say; No, you cannot come from this side. And the Zaka'ah(زكوة) would say; You cannot come from this side. And the other good deeds would say; You cannot come from next to the feet. And they would be making a shield; surrounding this person from every side; providing him with protection. Number two;

Seeking refuge in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى from the punishment of the grave.

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; When you make Tashahud(تشهّد), then seek refuge in Allah from four things. Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of hellfire, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of life and death, and from the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the false messiah; Ad-Dajjal(الدّجّال). So it is similar to say;

After Tashahud(تشهّد) and before Salam(سلام). In your Salah(صلوة); after you finish Al-Shahud(الشهّد), And then you say; These are four things, we should constantly seek refuge in Allah from. Who are the ones, who are spared from the trials of the grave Al-Fitnah(الفِتْنَه)? Who are the ones, who do not go through these trials. Number one; the top of the list; Ash-Shaheed(الشّهيد). Ash-Shaheed(الشّهيد); Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; There are six qualities for the Shaheed(شَهِيد). Six qualities. Number one; he would be forgiven with the first drop of blood, that comes out of his body. His sins would be forgiven. Number two; he would see his place in paradise. Number three; he would be saved from the punishment of the grave. Number four; he would be saved from the fear of the most fearful day; the day of judgment. Number five; the crown of tranquility will be placed on his head, one emerald in it; is worth, the world and everything in it. Number five; he would be married to 72 of Al-Hoor-ul-Een(الحور العين). And number six; he would be given intercession Shafa'ah(شفاعة) in 70 of his relatives. These are qualities, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given to the Shaheed(شَهِيد). One of the Sahabah(صحابه) said;

Oh Messenger of Allah! How come the believers go through the trials; the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the grave, but the Shaheed(شَهِيد) doesn't? Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

The shining of the swords over his head; is enough of a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for him. In the battlefield, when the swords are shining over his head, and that glimmering of light is reflected off the swords, and he see death in every moment; that is the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for the Shaheed(شَهِيد). But then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى would give him pleasure and tranquility in the grave. And today, we would say that, the same thing applies to the fire, the explosions, and the missiles, and the bullets; that pass next to the fighters; the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) in the sake of Allah; that is their Fitnah(فِتْنَه). But then, when they are killed in the sake of Allah; they would get pleasure in their graves. Because, they have run through enough. They have run through Fitnah(فِتْنَه), when they were in the middle of the battlefield. Number two;

Al-Murabit(المرابط) is the soldier, who is stationed in a position away from home; guarding the Muslims; waiting for instructions to fight. That is Al-Murabit(مرابط). It comes from Rabat(ربط). Rabat(ربط) was when you tie something. Al-Murabit(مرابط) is someone that is tied to that post. He cannot leave. It is as if you are tying a camel or horse. That guard; that soldier has to take that post, and has to guard it day and night. It's a very difficult job. Because of that; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is giving the Murabit(مرابط) a special reward. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Everyone; their deeds would be germinated the moment they die, except for the one who dies as a Murabit(مرابط), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى would continue his deeds for him, and they would keep on growing until the day of judgment, and he would be spared from the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of the grave. The reward of Ribat(رباط). Finally, there's a Hadith(حديث) mentioned that, the one who dies on the day of Jummah(جُمعَه) also get this honour. And this is a Hadith(حديث) that's Abu Hazam(ابو حازم), Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Any Muslim, who dies on Friday; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Would spare him from the punishment of the grave.
